course: dictionary
lesson: 10576
title: Uncut: not cut, and complete
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uncut is made of un-, which means not, and cut. Its simplest meaning is not cut: uncut grass is grass that nobody has mown. In «including uncut hair (kesh)», the hair has never been cut, and that is part of the promise.
explain: Uncut can also describe whole things. An uncut film or book has no parts taken out, so you see the full version. Look at the words around it: film, book or speech. Those words are the clue that uncut means complete.
explain: Uncut can describe stones too. An uncut gem has not yet been shaped and polished, so it can look like a dull stone. Ask yourself what is being talked about: hair, a film or a gem. That tells you which meaning fits, and you can check it by swapping your meaning into the sentence.
fact: Uncut means not cut: uncut grass, uncut hair, an uncut cake.
fact: Uncut can mean complete, with no parts taken out, as in «the uncut version of a film».
fact: An uncut gem has not yet been shaped and polished, so it can look like a dull stone.
fact: The words around uncut, such as film, hair or gem, tell you which meaning to use.
fact: The un- at the start of a word often means not, as in unhappy, unlock and uncut.
exercise: «The grass was still uncut, so it grew tall and wild.» What does uncut mean here? | *Not cut | Full of seeds | Cut very short | Painted green
exercise: «The shop sold the uncut version of the film, with every scene.» What does uncut mean here? | *Complete, with no parts taken out | Black and white | Shorter and cut down | Sold out
exercise: Mia says an uncut gem is a shiny jewel. Is she right? | Yes, because uncut means very expensive | Yes, it is already polished and ready to wear | *No, it has not been shaped or polished yet, so it can look dull
test: «Some Sikhs keep their hair uncut as part of their faith.» What does uncut mean? | Cut very short | Dyed a bright colour | Tied up in a bun | *Not cut
test: «A plastic drink ring that is still uncut can trap an animal.» What does uncut mean here? | Painted bright colours | Recycled and clean | *Still whole, not cut apart | Cut into small pieces
exam: Jayden says uncut always means something, like hair or grass, that has not been cut. Is he right? | *No, an uncut film means complete, with no parts taken out | No, uncut means the same as cut | Yes, that is the only meaning of uncut | Yes, but only for gems
